cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Torus in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Torus: A Configurable Systolic Array Generator in SpinalHDL"
abstract: >-
  Torus is a hardware generator for systolic arrays written in SpinalHDL.
  It supports three dataflow patterns (input stationary, weight stationary,
  and output stationary), signed and unsigned integer arithmetic, and freely
  configurable array dimensions and port bit widths.
type: software
